    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710a-88">

                <pb facs="0519" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg339"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Editor’s Note</hi></head>
                <p>—No minutes of this conversation have been found. The conversation and the
                    subject discussed are referred to, however, in the following memorandum of July
                    24 (in the Truman Papers) by Captain James K. Vardaman, Jr., Naval Aide to the
                    President: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Remind the President Wednesday morning to write a letter to Mr.
                            Churchill and send him a copy of telegram despatched to Generalissimo
                            Chiang Kai Shek and also copy of revised Lend Lease document read to
                            Churchill by Leahy on the porch this morning.”<anchor n="1"
                                xml:id="d710a-88-f1"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d710a-88-f1" n="1" xml:id="d710a-88-f1-content">
                <p>For the letter which was sent to Churchill on July 25, see <ref target="#d1183"
                        >documents Nos. 1183</ref> and <ref target="#d1248">1248</ref>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>. The “revised Lend Lease document” referred to
                    has not been identified. Cf. the enclosure to <ref target="#d1185">document No.
                        1185</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
